Skip four tests that cannot pass in a site build with CI set, or that are
unreliable independent of the installation:

- inductor/test_deterministic.py test_run2run_determinism: every variant runs
  benchmarks/dynamo/huggingface.py, which needs HuggingFace transformers and
  tries to pip-install it from GitHub at test time; the build has neither the
  package nor network access.
- test_serialization.py test_debug_set_in_ci: asserts that the PyTorch CI job
  exported TORCH_SERIALIZATION_DEBUG=1; it is enabled by any non-empty CI
  variable, which the build service sets.
- quantization test_learnable_forward_per_channel_cpu: the kernel and the
  Python reference disagree on inputs near 2**63 (integer overflow in the
  reference), see https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/111471.
- quantization test_fused_obs_fake_quant_moving_avg: draws torch.randn inside
  a Hypothesis test, so a replayed example uses different data; Hypothesis
  reports FlakyFailure on 1-ULP float16 differences on both A100 and H100.

Author: Rohit Goswami <rgoswami@ieee.org>

